WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Intent: open tcp/5432 from the user network to the database server (10.20.20.30)

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.800
make demo: the Batfish container is already running; waiting for Batfish to respond (real time)

3
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.600
kanit plan verifies two recorded proposals (--scripted, no model call) in Batfish, one after another

4
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.700
Round 1: REJECT. Round 2: ACCEPT. Report: kanit-rapor.md

5
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.700
Report: ACCEPTED after 2 rounds

6
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:37.700
Round 1 proposal: permit ip, all IP traffic to the database server

7
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:47.700
Violation: 10.10.10.0:49152 -> 10.20.20.30:22 TCP (SYN) is delivered (new violation). The SSH invariant breaks

8
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.700
Sample flows whose behaviour changed: ICMP now reaches the server too

9
00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:01.700
Round 2 proposal: tcp/5432 only (permit tcp ... eq 5432)

10
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:09.700
All four checks proved: three invariants and the proposal's tcp/5432 intent check

11
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:16.500
Result: the overly broad line was rejected with a counterexample, the narrow line accepted
